  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups><sharedRules><rule id="a74c-b16d-6804-ced3" name="They Killed the Father!" hidden="false">
      <description>If the Magus and Patriarch are both killed, at the moment the last has died all Brood Brother units and Hybrid Broods must take a Morale test with the following modifiers: -1 if the unit is &lt; 50% starting strength and -1 if the unit is pinned or falling back. If this test is passed, the unit is Fearless for the rest of the game. If it failed, the unit will Fall Back immediately, though they can regroup in later turns as normal.

If the unit was in combat when this Fall Back move occurs, the enemy unit may only Consolidate.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="263b-0275-dacc-4238" name="Our Father Watches Us, Let None Fail Him!" hidden="false">
      <description>All Brood Brother units with a model within 12" of the Magus or Patriarch count as having Leadership 10 for all Morale checks and tests to Regroup. These units can still test to Regroup, even if they are below 50% of starting strength or within 6" of an enemy unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7b06-16e4-067d-a5f5" name="Poor Maintenance" hidden="false">
      <description>After moving a Cult vehicle in the movement phase roll 2D6. On a roll of 2, the vehicle is immobilised the rest of the game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7480-6633-9906-f11b" name="Hypnotic Gaze" hidden="false">
      <description>Use during any Assault Phase after all models have moved but before any combat takes place. If the Cult psyker passes the Psychic Test, choose an enemy model in base contact. That model will need to roll 6's to hit in Assault that round. If the Psychic Test was successful, and the roll was higher than the enemy model's leadership, then the enemy cannot strike any blows at all.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b3e6-8d18-5e36-d27e" name="Rending Claws" hidden="false">
      <description>Any attacks which roll a 6 to hit wound automatically and ignore armour saves. When rolling to penetrate vehicle armour, if a 6 is rolled then the user can add an additional D6 to the score.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="df64-e7af-188e-83b3" name="Firebombs" hidden="false">
      <description>Firebombs work exactly like Frag Grenades, but prevent any assaulting Cultists from advancing. Any cult units involved in the assault may only consolidate. They also can only be used once per game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c8e6-e2a6-e887-5a21" name="Cult Relic" hidden="false">
      <description>If a unit carrying this Relic has just failed a Morale test and is falling back, after the Fall Back movement is resolved (but before the enemy decides to Consolidate or Pursue) it can take another Morale test to Regroup. Normal restrictions for Regrouping apply.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="7ff9-2ca7-9017-2bf2-9889a" name="Cocooned" page="98" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>The AP value of a wound caused by this weapon is the current Strength characteristic of the model it was allocated to.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8936-83d2-a0fc-7d64-9889a" name="Crush" page="99" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>A model equipped with a Metamorph claw has a +2 bonus to its Strength during the Fight subphase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5e06-11ab-8ac6-6375-9889a" name="Cult Ambush" page="96" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Units with this special rule that Infiltrate, or that arrive from Reserve or Ongoing Reserve, can chose to roll on the Cult Ambush table instead of deploying or arriving from Reserves normally. Unless otherwise specified, ambushing units move onto the table as described for other Reserves and cannot move any further during the movement phase. Units cannot use the cult ambush special rule whilst they are embarked inside a vehicle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c1c1-1f74-d087-a7ae-9889a" name="Lash" page="99" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>A model equipped with a aweapon with this special rule has +3 Initiative during the Fight subphase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="39c4-8377-613e-d833-9889a" name="Life Drain" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Any To Wound roll of 6 made with this weapon has the Instant Death (see BRB) USR.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="abd2-de87-26fb-c254-9889a" name="Pulverise" page="99" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>When a model with a heavy rock drill makes its close combat attacks, it can instead make a single pulverise attack. If it does so, roll To Hit as normal, but resolve the hit at S10 AP1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7076-ce81-4717-92db-9889a" name="Resonance" page="98" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>To Wound and Armour Penetration rolls of 6 made with a weapon with this special rule are resolved at AP1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="68a1-1058-e764-744e-9889a" name="Return to the Shadows" page="96" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Instead of moving in the movement phase, any unit with this special rule that is not within 6" of any enemy models, can be removed from the battlefield and placed into Ongoing Reserve. A unit cannot Return to the Shadows in the same turn it arrives from Reserves or Ongoing Reserves, and cannot do so whilst embarked in a vehicle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7ae4-44e1-0be4-896c-9889a" name="Scythe" page="99" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>A model equipped with a Metamorph talon has a +1 bonus to Weapon Skill during the Fight subphase. A model equipped with two Metamorph talons has a +2 bonus to Weapon Skill during the Fight subphase instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1219-8219-ab18-839a-9889a" name="Snip" page="99" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>When a model suffers one or more unsaved Wounds from this weapon, it must pass a seperate Toughness test for each Wound suffered or be removed from play.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="890d-2f13-d09f-5149-9889a" name="Unquestioning Loyalty" page="96" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>A model with this special rule automatically passes Look Out, Sir attempts, and can even make Look Out, Sir attempts when fighting in a challenge.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules><sharedProfiles><profile id="7626-8fa0-f433-5dba" name="Genestealer Magus" hidden="false" typeId="1e16-2bd8-7cad-379b" typeName="Unit">
